      "problem": "What is the solution to the equation $0.25s=0.5?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $100$ to get rid of the decimals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.25s & =0.5 \\\\ 100\\cdot (0.25s) & =100\\cdot (0.5) \\\\ 25s & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the equation using the multiplication principle, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25s & =50 \\\\ \\frac{25s}{25} & =\\frac{50}{25} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{25}s}{\\cancel{25}} & =\\frac{50}{25} \\\\ s & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
